ECP5-2ADC-2DAC is open hardware and open source.

  Hardware   CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive (CERN-OHL-P-2.0)
             The schematic, the PCB, the generator scripts' design data, the
             manufacturing files, the drawings and renders, and the
             documentation of how to make and bring up the board
             (the KiCad project, gen/, pcb/, library/, mfg/, docs/, photos/,
             the design documents).
             Full text: LICENSE-HARDWARE.txt

  Software   MIT License (below)
             The gateware, the host programs, the bench and bring-up programs,
             and the build, simulation and check scripts
             (gateware/, bringup/, sim/, tools/, build.py).

Both licences are permissive: you may make, sell, modify and share the board
and its derivatives, keeping the copyright and licence notices.

ECP5-2ADC-2DAC is a Lattice ECP5 board with two ADC channels, two DAC
channels and gigabit Ethernet, open from the schematic to the Linux that runs
on its RISC-V soft core.  Designed by Jason Gallicchio with Claude
(Anthropic's Claude Code), October and November 2026.

Third-party material:
  * Symbols, footprints and 3D models copied from the KiCad libraries are
    CC-BY-SA 4.0 with the KiCad libraries' exception: using them in a design
    does not put the design under CC-BY-SA.
  * library/easyeda/ holds symbols and footprints converted from EasyEDA's
    parts library (JLCPCB's land patterns and pin tables) with easyeda2kicad.
    Their 3D models are not part of this repository.
  * gateware/litex/ecp5_2adc_2dac.py is a generated LiteX platform file,
    BSD-2-Clause like litex-boards.
  * Datasheets are not part of this repository (datasheets/ is ignored), and
    neither are the copies of them the design reviewers made.  Lattice's
    pinout table, which gen/fpga.py reads, is among them.
  * The reports under design_review/ were written by the language models and
    review services named there, at the author's request.
  * The FPGA is built with Yosys, nextpnr and Project Trellis, which are not
    part of this repository.

